    name: 'Nevada "American Tax Service" Tax-Debt Settlement Scam',
    slug: 'nevada-american-tax-service-tax-relief-settlement',
    description: `Nevada Attorney General Aaron Ford announced a settlement on June 3, 2026 resolving a consumer-protection lawsuit against Terrance Selb, Tyler Bennett, and a web of companies they ran under names including American Tax Service, American Tax Solutions, ATS Tax Group LLC, Elite Sales Solutions, GetATaxLawyer.com LLC, and several TNT-branded entities, requiring the defendants to surrender nearly $10 million in cash and other assets for consumer relief. The office alleged the defendants marketed themselves nationally as tax-debt relief specialists, falsely promising consumers — especially older adults — that their operation could settle IRS or state tax debt for "pennies on the dollar," while in reality signing clients up without any real evaluation of whether they qualified for such a reduction, then pressuring many into tens of thousands of dollars in expensive add-on services that delivered little or nothing of value. Court filings found consumers paid the defendants roughly $77.7 million between February 2022 and 2025, and some communications and collection tactics allegedly mimicked actual tax authorities to make the pitch feel more official and urgent. "Consumers who are struggling with tax debt deserve honest information and legitimate assistance, not false promises," Ford said in announcing the settlement. Nevadans and other consumers considering a tax-relief company are advised to be skeptical of any guaranteed "pennies on the dollar" promise made before a real review of their specific tax situation, to verify a company's standing with the Better Business Bureau and their state attorney general before paying anything, and to consider contacting the IRS or a state tax agency directly, which can often set up a legitimate payment plan at no cost. Complaints can be filed with the Nevada Attorney General's Bureau of Consumer Protection at ag.nv.gov.`,
